---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Visual from '../components/Visual.astro';
import ToolCard from '../components/ToolCard.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { repository } from '../lib';
const tools=(await getCollection('tools')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
---
<Base>
<section class="hero section-shell"><div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN SOURCE · BUILT FOR EVERYDAY USE</div><h1>CFD indicators.<br/><span>Browser tools.</span></h1><p class="hero-description">See exchange share data on your CFD chart, customise TradingView in your browser, and add Trade Nation shortcuts and statistics. Four indicators and six userscripts, with setup guides and source code.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="/indicators/">Explore indicators <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button secondary" href="/userscripts/">Browse userscripts</a></div><div class="hero-facts"><span><b>04</b> Pine indicators</span><span><b>06</b> Browser tools</span><span><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m4 10 4 4 8-8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg> Setup guides included</span></div></div><div class="hero-art"><div class="floating-chip"><span class="status-dot"></span> CFD CHART <span aria-hidden="true">↔</span> UNDERLYING MARKET</div><Visual kind="overview" capture="A CFD chart with Info, selected percentage levels and the mapped source visible."/><div class="hero-art-note"><span>01 / CFD CHART WITH MAPPED DATA</span><span>Illustrated workspace</span></div></div></section>
<div class="context-band"><div class="section-shell"><span>Company and earnings data.</span><span>Share, futures and ETF volume.</span><span>Percentage levels on CFDs.</span><a href="/about/">Why these tools exist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
<section class="section-shell section-space" id="indicators"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / INDICATORS</div><h2>Company data, volume<br/>and CFD price levels.</h2></div><div><p>Match a CFD to its exchange or reference symbol, then show company information, selected volume or percentage levels on the chart. Built in Pine for TradingView.</p><a href="/indicators/" class="text-link">All indicators & setup <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><a class="setup-strip" href="/tools/symbol-mapper/"><div class="map-icon" aria-hidden="true">⇄</div><div><span class="mini-label">START HERE · SYMBOL MAPPER</span><h3>Share symbol mappings between indicators.</h3><p>Use shared mapping when your indicator needs it. Keep existing local maps and formulas when it does not.</p></div><span class="circle-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="tool-grid three">{tools.filter(t=>['info','real-volume','cfd-levels'].includes(t.id)).map(tool=><ToolCard tool={tool}/>)}</div></section>
<section class="browser-section section-space"><div class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / USERSCRIPTS</div><h2>Customise TradingView<br/>in your browser.</h2></div><div><p>Name your tabs, click recognised tickers, open saved AI questions for the current symbol and see watchlist prices on hover.</p><a href="/userscripts/" class="text-link">All browser & broker tools <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="browser-feature"><div><span class="outline-label">TRADINGVIEW WEBSITE · DESKTOP BROWSER</span><h3>See watchlist prices<br/>on hover.</h3><p>Keep the percentage in your watchlist. Hover to see a price. These four enhancements run through a browser userscript manager, not inside TradingView Desktop.</p><a href="/tools/watchlist/" class="button secondary">Explore Watchlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="small-copy">Edge or Chrome + Tampermonkey is the current workflow.</p></div><Visual kind="watchlist" capture="The same watchlist badge before and during hover, with one ordinary row showing its Last price."/></div><div class="compact-links">{tools.filter(t=>t.data.group==='tradingview'&&t.id!=='watchlist').map(t=><a href={`/tools/${t.id}/`}><span>{t.data.label}</span><b>{t.data.name.replace('SVKO TradingView ','')} <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i></b><p>{t.data.summary}</p></a>)}</div><div class="broker-teaser"><div><div class="eyebrow">ALSO IN USERSCRIPTS / TRADE NATION</div><h3>Trade Nation hotkeys and statistics.</h3></div><div><a href="/tools/trade-nation-hotkeys/">Hotkeys <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/tools/trading-statistics/">Trading Statistics <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section-shell section-space"><div class="open-source-panel" data-reveal><div class="source-glyph" aria-hidden="true">&lt;/&gt;</div><div><div class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE, OPEN TO IMPROVEMENT</div><h2>Read the source.<br/>Report bugs or contribute.</h2><p>Read the source, report something that does not work, or propose a change. Each tool links to its code and licence.</p><a class="button primary" href={repository}>Explore on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="source-details"><span>Public source</span><span>Practical documentation</span><span>Issues & pull requests</span><a href="/about/#licences">Licences and attribution ↗</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
